implementationPlan.description:
VERIFY ONCE, fresh.

1. Run the DoD command, `node --test scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs`. It must exit 0; supply its command, exit code and output tail to complete_task. On WSL, run it as `env -i HOME="$HOME" PATH="<linux node bin>:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin" node --test scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs` with no MOE_* set. python3 must be on PATH, for the real-supervisor tests.
2. ALSO run, and report: `node --test scripts/tests/local-runner-check.test.mjs scripts/tests/local-runner-vm-control.test.mjs scripts/tests/local-runner-snapshot.test.mjs`. These are the other suites that import lifecycle.mjs, provision.mjs or the check modules.
3. Mutants, on scratch copies only; restore and cmp afterwards. Each must fail a named case:
   (i) skip the bootstrapReady check: CJ3;
   (ii) remove only on the happy path: CJ3 and CJ4;
   (iii) settle before remove: CJ5;
   (iv) pass the owner's ledger unwrapped to provision: CJ8's throw-after-reserve row;
   (v) use the observed memoryTotal instead of GUEST_RESOURCES: CJ2's environment equality;
   (vi) delete a collision record in deleteOwned: its test;
   (vii) report 'passed' after a failed delete: CJ6.

comments.content:
Architect split, 2026-10-29. The human chose in the architect REPL: **one fresh owned VM per check run**, deleted after it.

This row is now the orchestrator and keeps its DoD 1-4. It is BLOCKED until its slices are DONE, then it returns to PLANNING. Plan it against their landed code:
- CQ-R11d (task-874aa17c): CHECK_BOUNDARIES, checkEnvironment and evidenceStatus, in the new check-evidence.mjs and local-runner-check.test.mjs (added to CI). It owns DoD 3 and the "reported" half of DoD 2.
- CQ-R11a (task-37dd3edb): the guest `check` mode. One frame; the job runs as moe-check with no groups, NoNewPrivs, umask 077, an exact environment, rlimits and a private network namespace. It owns the "enforced" half of DoD 2.
- CQ-R11b (task-9048e7ec): protected-path oids verified before and after the run, plus read-only bind mounts. It owns the "mutate protected definitions" half of DoD 1.
- CQ-R11c (task-53daa94f): the host runCheckSession, the CheckOutcome classification and a bounded outputTail.
- CQ-R11e (task-001d8ab3, BACKLOG): the guest check toolchain, a human decision. CQ-R13 now depends on it; this row does not, because it proves the lifecycle with python3 stdlib checks.

What remains for this row is the orchestration for one check:
1. provision a fresh owned VM (R03/R04/R05 provisionGuest plus the R06 ledger);
2. waitForGuestReady (R07: the supervisor hash, and every job identity denied the supervisor credential, which is the "credential" half of DoD 1);
3. assertNoMounts, then materializeSnapshot (R09c);
4. runCheckSession (R11c);
5. delete the VM on every path (R06);
6. return an observation carrying R11d's checkEnvironment.
Details are in Serena `decision-cq-r11-split`.

executionContract.intendedBehavior:
One isolated check runs in one fresh owned VM.

runCheckJob does the following, in order:
- provisions a fresh VM and requires clean R07 readiness, whose probes deny every job identity the supervisor credential;
- materializes the snapshot with no mounts;
- reports the environment identity (checkEnvironment over CHECK_BOUNDARIES, the observed image and supervisor, and GUEST_RESOURCES) to the caller's onReady hook before the session;
- runs the approved check through runCheckSession, whose R11a/R11b guest mode enforces the identity, network, rlimit and protected-path boundaries;
- deletes the VM before it settles, on every path.

Outcomes use CheckOutcome. A passed run whose VM was not deleted is inconclusive. workspace stays 'unverified' until CQ-R11f.

